   5:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** /*
   6:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	Use an AA-tree to quickly look up properties in objects:
   7:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 
   8:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	The level of every leaf node is one.
   9:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	The level of every left child is one less than its parent.
  10:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	The level of every right child is equal or one less than its parent.
  11:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	The level of every right grandchild is less than its grandparent.
  12:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	Every node of level greater than one has two children.
  13:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 
  14:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	A link where the child's level is equal to that of its parent is called a horizontal link.
  15:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	Individual right horizontal links are allowed, but consecutive ones are forbidden.
  16:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	Left horizontal links are forbidden.
  17:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 
  18:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	skew() fixes left horizontal links.
  19:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** 	split() fixes consecutive right horizontal links.
  20:Source/js/jsproperty.c **** */
